			"date": "2023-12-14T14:42:09.129Z",
			"content": "<p>I see this experimental limbo for Node.js’ ESM `vm.Module` causing large scale problems elsewhere too, right?</p><p>Jest seems to be trying to stick to Node.js APIs (which is a good goal!) and people are migrating to Vitest for “stable” ESM support—but Vitest is using `esbuild` to sidestep the experimental status.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111579323966021833",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://c.im/@matthewp/111579323918169847",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matthew Phillips",
				"url": "https://c.im/@matthewp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/319/884/743/792/129/original/97348f81981453d9.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-12-14T14:49:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I wouldn't count on VM / realms stuff, they've been unstable in a number of ways for 10+ years.</p><p>Do workers fulfill your needs?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111579792986075650",
			"parentId": "111579295195494761",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/111579792986075650",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
